{%- comment -%}
  The products carousel of the predictive-search recommendations panel, fetched on demand by
  search.js the first time a pointer or focus reaches the search form.

  It is the only part of that panel worth deferring: measured on the demo store it is 85,638 of
  the panel's 87,127 bytes and every one of its product images — `predictive-search.liquid`
  renders the panel on every page twice (header search + search drawer) for something nobody has
  opened, it made the browser fetch all 8 images at ~1.5s, and it rode along in every
  per-keystroke section render only to be discarded. The keywords beside it are 1,489 bytes with
  no media, so they stay inline.

  The `data-recommendations-content` wrapper is the morph host: `revealSwap` swaps this element
  for the placeholder of the same name, so the attributes on both sides must stay identical.

  The column/gap constants mirror `predictive-search.liquid`. `media_sizes` uses the header
  panel's width: a section cannot read query params, so one endpoint serves both contexts, and
  the drawer's slightly narrower column (156px vs 164px) resolves to the same srcset candidate.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign columns_xxl = 3
  assign columns_xl = columns_xxl | at_most: 4
  assign columns_lg = columns_xxl | at_most: 3
  assign columns_md = columns_xxl | at_most: 3
  assign columns_mobile = 2
  assign column_gap = 10
  assign column_gap_mobile = 8
-%}
{%- capture media_sizes -%}
  (min-width: 768px) calc((min(100vw, 554px) - 60px) / {{ columns_xxl }}), calc(min(500px, 100vw) * 0.38)
{%- endcapture -%}
<div data-recommendations-content>
  {% render 'predictive-search-recommendation-products-markup',
    columns_xxl: columns_xxl,
    columns_xl: columns_xl,
    columns_lg: columns_lg,
    columns_md: columns_md,
    columns_mobile: columns_mobile,
    column_gap: column_gap,
    column_gap_mobile: column_gap_mobile,
    media_sizes: media_sizes
  %}
</div>
